  "question": {
    "text": "Consider circles <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> &amp; <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> touching both the axes and passing through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the product of radii of these circles is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "32",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since circle touches both the axes and passes through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, it lies in the first quadrant, so its equation is<br /><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on it hence<br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Hence, the product of roots (radii) <math><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></math>",
    "image": null
  },
